n the 2025 Longines Breeders’ Cup Turf (G1) at odds of 27-1. \r\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThis year, Ethical Diamond has won the Aug. 6 Ballyroan Stakes (G3) at Leopardstown in Ireland, and he finished second in the Sept. 5 Kentucky Turf Cup Invitational \u0026nbsp;(G2) at Kentucky Downs behind Tiffany (IRE). He also finished fifth in the March 28 Longines Dubai Sheema Classic (G1) and ninth in the June 20 Hardwicke Stakes (G2). \r\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eLast year, before the Breeders’ Cup, Ethical Diamond won the Duke Of Edinburgh Stakes at Royal Ascot and the Ebor Handicap at York. \r\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eEthical Diamond, who has also competed in jumps racing, is conditioned by Willie Mullins, the renowned jumps trainer who also runs horses on the flat. Ethical Diamond began 2025 in hurdle races. \u0026nbsp;\r\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn 2024, Ethical Diamond did not find the winner’s circle. In 2023, he broke his maiden in his third attempt. He did not race as a 2-year-old. \u0026nbsp;\r\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eEthical Diamond is owned by the H O S Syndicate. It was set up by Irish businesswoman Margaret Heffernan, who established the syndicate for her grandchildren. \r\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eW. J. Kennedy bred Ethical Diamond. The 6-year-old gelding is by Awtaad (IRE) and out of the Areion (GER) mare Pearl Diamond (GER).\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e","gradedStakesPoints":0,"regionWinnerBadges":[],"breederName":"Mr W. J. Kennedy","uid":"blt0d5c17ed85f3b91a","hasAutogeneratedPage":true,"url":"/redirect/horse/blt0d5c17ed85f3b91a?ht=pre-entries","pageTitle":"Ethical Diamond (IRE)","jockeyName":"","ownerName":"HOS Syndicate (Margaret Heffernan)","trainer":"Willie Mullins","country":{"uid":"blta32e5b692b12a246","title":"Ireland","abbreviation":"IRE","flag":{"src":"https://images.contentstack.io/v3/assets/blt9b0ea57b1efe7a70/blt613f9a736c40223a/61aa4c2b2f8b9e70946988d3/ireland.png","alt":""}},"horseName":"Ethical Diamond","avatar":{"src":"https://images.conte