in":3,"place":3,"showP":"11","winP":"17","placeP":"17"}},"yearlySummary":[{"showsP":"0","winsP":"29","placesP":"43","starts":7,"earnings":264776,"racingYear":2026,"shows":0,"wins":2,"places":3},{"showsP":"NA","winsP":"NA","placesP":"NA","starts":0,"earnings":0,"racingYear":2025,"shows":0,"wins":0,"places":0}],"morningLineOdds":[],"bio":"\u003cp\u003eOn Sept. 6, Telescopic scored the biggest victory of his career at Kentucky Downs. Sent off as the betting favorite in a field of 11, the 5-year-old gelding took the lucrative 1 ½-mile allowance race by 2 lengths over The Brigade. \r\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eOff that victory, Telescopic headed to Churchill Downs where he won another allowance race on Sept. 27. Once again sent off as the race favorite, he defeated Clyde’s Got a Gun by 2 ¾ lengths in the 1 3/8-mile contest. Telescopic had finished second in three other allowance races this year prior to his victories. He also had two fourth-place finishes in the same company. \u0026nbsp;\r\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eTelescopic did not race in 2025. In 2024, he finished fourth in the Hawthorne Derby. As a juvenile in 2023, he made one start that December at Turfway Park and was off the board. \r\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eVicki Oliver trains Telescopic for BBN Racing. The partnership group bought him for $150,000 at the 2022 Keeneland September yearling sale. \r\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWesterberg Ireland ULC bred Telescopic. The gelding is by American Pharoah and out of the Galileo (IRE) mare Visage (IRE).\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e","gradedStakesPoints":0,"regionWinnerBadges":[],"breederName":"Westerberg Ireland ULC","uid":"blt2dfc9a15fec5f329","hasAutogeneratedPage":true,"url":"/redirect/horse/blt2dfc9a15fec5f329?ht=pre-entries","pageTitle":"Telescopic","jockeyName":"","ownerName":"BBN Racing, LLC (Ann Braxton Lynch)","trainer":"Vicki Oliver","country":{"uid":"blt1af49e3a6a89373f","title":"USA","abbreviation":"USA","flag":{"src":"https://images.contentstack.io/v3/assets/bl