l Clement has been around world-class horses all his life and hasn't missed a beat since taking over the reins of a talent-laden stable from his late father, Christophe Clement. So when he sings the praises of his star turf runner, Deterministic, the plaudits are meaningful. \r\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eSo is the performance put up by the 5-year-old son of Liam's Map. After winning the Fourstardave (G1) at Saratoga for the second straight year Aug. 8, Deterministic boasted a six-race winning streak, four at the Grade I level. \r\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\"He's just special. I can't say enough,\" Clement said after the second Fourstardave win. \r\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eDeterministic was unable to accept a \"Win and You're In\" Challenge bid to the 2025 FanDuel Breeders' Cup Mile (G1) because of a season-ending setback. Clement and the ownership group headed by St. Elias Stable hope to plug that gap in Deterministic's resume at Keeneland as he qualified for the big race again with the Saratoga victory. \r\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eDeterministic had his winning streak snapped in the Woodbine Mile (G1) on Sept. 12 when he was collared in deep stretch by defending race champion and 2025 FanDuel Breeders’ Cup Mile (G1) winner Notable Speech (GB) who prevailed by 1 1/4 lengths. \r\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eDeterministic's sire, Liam's Map, capped his career in 2015 with an impressive win at Keeneland in the Las Vegas Breeders' Cup Dirt Mile (G1). His dam, the Speightstown mare Giulio's Jewel, was a three-time winner sprinting on turf. \r\u003c/p\u003e","gradedStakesPoints":3,"regionWinnerBadges":[],"breederName":"Hinkle Farms","uid":"blt1c3d34d8d469b9e6","hasAutogeneratedPage":true,"url":"/redirect/horse/blt1c3d34d8d469b9e6?ht=pre-entries","pageTitle":"Deterministic","jockeyName":"","ownerName":"St. Elias Stables (Vincent Viola), Ken Langone, C. Steven Duncker and Vicarage Stable (Kevin Warsh)","trainer":"Miguel Clement","country":{"uid":"blt1af49e3a6a89373f","title":"