NTA ANITA PARK","raceName":" ","grade":" ","raceDate":"February, 24 2024 00:00:00","purseUsa":67000,"positionAtFinish":2},{"trackName":"SANTA ANITA PARK","raceName":"San Vicente S.","grade":"2","raceDate":"January, 06 2024 00:00:00","purseUsa":200000,"positionAtFinish":6},{"trackName":"SANTA ANITA PARK","raceName":"Zuma Beach S.","grade":"3","raceDate":"October, 08 2023 00:00:00","purseUsa":200000,"positionAtFinish":6},{"trackName":"DEL MAR","raceName":" ","grade":" ","raceDate":"September, 10 2023 00:00:00","purseUsa":82000,"positionAtFinish":1}],"record":{"previousYear":{"starts":6,"earnings":868000,"show":0,"win":3,"place":1,"showP":"0","winP":"50","placeP":"17"},"breedersCup":{"starts":1,"earnings":340000,"show":0,"win":0,"place":1,"showP":"0","winP":"0","placeP":"100"},"currentYear":{"starts":3,"earnings":229000,"show":1,"win":1,"place":0,"showP":"33","winP":"33","placeP":"0"},"lifetime":{"starts":19,"earnings":1734425,"show":1,"win":9,"place":3,"showP":"5","winP":"47","placeP":"16"}},"yearlySummary":[{"showsP":"33","winsP":"33","placesP":"0","starts":3,"earnings":229000,"racingYear":2026,"shows":1,"wins":1,"places":0},{"showsP":"0","winsP":"50","placesP":"17","starts":6,"earnings":868000,"racingYear":2025,"shows":0,"wins":3,"places":1}],"morningLineOdds":[],"bio":"\u003cp\u003eFormidable Man is quite appropriately named, particularly when he's set the task of covering 1 mile on the grass. When the 5-year-old son of City of Light won the Shoemaker Mile (G1) on May 25, he improved his career scorecard to 9 wins and 3 seconds from 17 starts. \u0026nbsp;\r\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eTrainer Michael McCarthy obviously knew what he had in Formidable Man from the start and backed his instincts by entering him in the 1-mile Zuma Beach Stakes (G3) for 2-year-olds on the Santa Anita turf in just his second start. He pressed the pace before finishing sixth but was on his way. \r\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eFrom there, he has won such classy events as the Del Mar Derby (G1) and the Hollywood Derby (G1), both at 1 1/8 miles. Victories in 2025 in the Frank E. Kilroe Mile (G1) and the Del Mar Mile (G2) plus the Eddie Read (G2) at 1 1/8 miles led him to the FanDuel Breeders' Cup Mile (G1) at Del Mar, where he finished second, behind Godolphin's Notable Speech (GB). \u0026nbsp;\r\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eBack at Del Mar for his next start after the Shoemaker, Formidable Man was third in a three-horse photo for the win in his bid to repeat in the Eddie Read on July 26. \r\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eHeading east to Kentucky Downs for the Mint Millions (G3) on Sept. 7, Formidable Man never was a factor and checked in seventh in the field of 10 beaten 4 3/4 lengths. \r\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eBred by Town \u0026amp; Country Horse Farms LLC, Formidable Man was produced by the Silent Name (JPN) mare Fanticola. He races for William and Suzanne Warren.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e","gradedStakesPoints":12,"regionWinnerBadges":[],"breederName":"Town \u0026 Country Horse Farms, LLC","uid":"blt413ad76294433a53","hasAutogeneratedPage":true,"url":"/redirect/horse/blt413ad76294433a53?ht=pre-entries","pageTitle":"Formidable Man","jockeyName":"","ownerName":"William K. Warren, Jr. \u0026 Suzanne Warren","trainer":"Michael W. McCarthy","country":{"uid":"blt1af49e3a6a89373f","title":"USA","abbreviation":"USA","flag":{"src":"https://images.contentstack.io/v3/assets/blt9b0ea57b1efe7a70/blt9de45bbdff160673/60d219911e0505677a882fa1/USAFlag.png"}},"horseName":"Formidable Man","avatar":{"src":"https://images.contentstack.io/v3/assets/blt9b0ea57b1efe7a70/blt1bfe2f7608030a0b/6a739bc9c5d6fd1980957130/Contender_Photo_Formidable_Man.jpg"},"regularImage":{"src":"https://images.contentstack.io/v3/assets/blt9b0ea57b1efe7a70/blt1bfe2f7608030a0b/6a739bc9c5d6fd1980957130/Contender_Photo_Formidable_Man.jpg"},"cta":null,"races":[{"uid":"blt31ae65439327eecf","ContentTypeUid":"collection_race","challengeSeriesWinner":false,"isEligible":false,"eligibleRank":null,"finishPosition":nu