0","purseUsa":60000,"positionAtFinish":1}],"record":{"previousYear":{"starts":5,"earnings":728900,"show":1,"win":1,"place":1,"showP":"20","winP":"20","placeP":"20"},"breedersCup":{"starts":3,"earnings":240000,"show":1,"win":0,"place":0,"showP":"33","winP":"0","placeP":"0"},"currentYear":{"starts":3,"earnings":306500,"show":0,"win":1,"place":0,"showP":"0","winP":"33","placeP":"0"},"lifetime":{"starts":28,"earnings":2297426,"show":7,"win":8,"place":4,"showP":"25","winP":"29","placeP":"14"}},"yearlySummary":[{"showsP":"0","winsP":"33","placesP":"0","starts":3,"earnings":306500,"racingYear":2026,"shows":0,"wins":1,"places":0},{"showsP":"20","winsP":"20","placesP":"20","starts":5,"earnings":728900,"racingYear":2025,"shows":1,"wins":1,"places":1}],"morningLineOdds":[],"bio":"\u003cp\u003eSeven-year-old Nakatomi will be trying the Cygames Breeders’ Cup Sprint (G1) for the fourth consecutive year after notching his best result when third in 2023 at Santa Anita. On Oct. 2, he captured the “Win And You’re In” Phoenix Stakes (G2) at Keeneland for the second consecutive time. \u0026nbsp;\r\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eTrainer Wesley Ward attributes Nakatomi’s longevity to his annual vacation at a farm near his Keeneland base where he enjoys attention from teenaged Ell-Marie Galvin, daughter of Fergus Galvin, racing manager for co-owner Qatar’s U.S. division. She grooms and sometimes rides him. \u0026nbsp;\r\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e“When horses get those winters off, they come back mentally fresh,” Ward said. \r\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eNakatomi first flashed his brilliance in his debut as 2-year-old at the 2021 Keeneland April meeting and has been a force in the upper echelons since. The gelding has collected nearly $2.3 million in 28 starts with an 8-4-7 record that includes a Grade 1 victory in the 2024 Alfred G. Vanderbilt at Saratoga. \r\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eHe has changed hands three times at public auction starting as an $18,000 weaning at the 2019 Keeneland November sale. He then was sold for $25,000 at Fasig-Tipton’s October yearling sale in Lexington, Kentucky to Marc Detampel, who campaigned him solely and later in partnership with Qatar Racing and others. The partnership was dissolved when current owners Qatar Racing and Mrs. Fitriani Hay purchased Nakatomi for $205,000 at the 2023 Fasig-Tipton July Horses of Racing Age Sale. \r\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eNakatomi’s sire Firing Line finished second to American Pharoah in the 2015 Kentucky Derby (G1). \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e","gradedStakesPoints":6,"regionWinnerBadges":[],"breederName":"Arnold Zetcher LLC \u0026 Crestwood Farm","uid":"blt92c75696ab75a706","hasAutogeneratedPage":true,"url":"/redirect/horse/blt92c75696ab75a706?ht=pre-entries","pageTitle":"Nakatomi","jockeyName":"","ownerName":"Qatar Racing LLC (Sheikh Fahad al Thani) and Fitriani Hay","trainer":"Wesley A. Ward","country":{"uid":"blt1af49e3a6a89373f","title":"USA","abbreviation":"USA","flag":{"src":"https://images.contentstack.io/v3/assets/blt9b0ea57b1efe7a70/blt9de45bbdff160673/60d219911e0505677a882fa1/USAFlag.png"}},"horseName":"Nakatomi","avatar":{"src":"https://images.contentstack.io/v3/assets/blt9b0ea57b1efe7a70/bltbc44279e20757302/68e7e603c73dc90d1e552dd9/Contender_Photo_Nakatomi.jpg"},"regularImage":{"src":"https://images.contentstack.io/v3/assets/blt9b0ea57b1efe7a70/bltbc44279e20757302/68e7e603c73dc90d1e552dd9/Contender_Photo_Nakatomi.jpg"},"cta":null,"races":[{"uid":"bltf6749e738cff0ef2","ContentTypeUid":"collection_race","challengeSeriesWinner":false,"isEligible":false,"eligibleRank":null,"finishPosition":null,"classicRanking":null,"postPosition":"","scratched":false,"win":"","place":"","show":"","deadHeat":false,"silks":null}],"isChallengeSeriesWinner":true,"silks":null,"isHoC":false,"year":2026,"isHistoricalEntry":false,"relatedArticles":[],"win":"","show":"","place":""},{"sireName":"Prospective","damName":"Nina's Gift","sex":"Gelding","color":"Gray or Roan","foalingDate":"April, 21 2020 00:00:00"