:1,"win":10,"place":8,"showP":"4","winP":"40","placeP":"32"}},"yearlySummary":[{"showsP":"0","winsP":"33","placesP":"67","starts":3,"earnings":229550,"racingYear":2026,"shows":0,"wins":1,"places":2},{"showsP":"0","winsP":"67","placesP":"11","starts":9,"earnings":551145,"racingYear":2025,"shows":0,"wins":6,"places":1}],"morningLineOdds":[],"bio":"\u003cp\u003eRoll On Big Joe returned to the work tab in September after spending the summer on the sidelines.\r\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe 6-year-old gelding has not started since inching his way closer to the million-dollar earnings mark by finishing second in the Aristides Stakes (G3) at Churchill Downs on May 30. Six weeks prior, he was runner-up in the Count Fleet Sprint Handicap (G3) to Mad House, who went on to be a close third behind Cygames Breeders’ Cup Sprint (G1) contender Nakatomi in the “Win and You’re In” Phoenix Stakes (G2) at Keeneland. \r\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eRemarkably consistent throughout his career except when well beaten in his only turf attempt, Roll On Big Joe has capitalized on his earnings power as a standout competitor in stakes and allowance races. His scores at that level include two Grade 3 events last year and three other stakes.\r\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e“The owners were patient with him when he was young and allowed him to go through some growing pains,” trainer Bob Hess said after Roll On Big Joe won the 2025 Palos Verdes Stakes (G3) in 2025. \u0026nbsp;\r\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eRoll On Big Joe was purchased by current co-owner Rancho Temescal for $90,000 at the 2022 Ocala Breeders’ Sales Co. 2-year-olds in training sale. \r\u003c/p\u003e","gradedStakesPoints":4,"regionWinnerBadges":[],"breederName":"Max Ubide","uid":"bltd6921cf5c5d3daf7","hasAutogeneratedPage":true,"url":"/redirect/horse/bltd6921cf5c5d3daf7?ht=pre-entries","pageTitle":"Roll On Big Joe","jockeyName":"","ownerName":"Rancho Temescal (Tim Cohen), Rancho Temescal Thoroughbred Partners (Joseph Miller), Richard T. Hale \u0026 White Fence LLC (David Marabella)","trainer":"Robert B. Hess Jr.","country":{"uid":"blt1af49e3a6a89373f","title":"USA","abbreviation":"USA","flag":{"src":"https://images.contentstack.io/v3/assets/blt9b0ea57b1efe7a70/blt9de45bbdff160673/60d219911e0505677a882fa1/USAFlag.png"}},"horseName":"Roll On Big Joe","avatar":{"src":"https://images.contentstack.io/v3/assets/blt9b0ea57b1efe7a70/blt9bc8fab8b1c77b0f/6aabf6dda81298c20be3e69b/Contender_Photo_Roll_On_Big_Joe.jpg"},"regularImage":{"src":"https://images.contentstack.io/v3/assets/blt9b0ea57b1efe7a70/blt9bc8fab8b1c77b0f/6aabf6dda81298c20be3e69b/Contender_Photo_Roll_On_Big_Joe.jpg"},"cta":null,"races":[{"uid":"bltf6749e738cff0ef2","ContentTypeUid":"collection_race","challengeSeriesWinner":false,"isEligible":false,"eligibleRank":null,"finishPosition":null,"classicRanking":null,"postPosition":"","scratched":false,"win":"","place":"","show":"","deadHeat":false,"silks":null}],"isChallengeSeriesWinner":false,"silks":null,"isHoC":false,"year":2026,"isHistoricalEntry":false,"relatedArticles":[],"win":"","show":"","place":""},{"sireName":"Yaupon","damName":"Twitterpated","sex":"Colt","color":"Bay","foalingDate":"February, 07 2023 00:00:00","age":3,"pastPerformances":[{"trackName":"PARX RACING","raceName":"Gallant Bob S.","grade":"2","raceDate":"September, 19 2026 00:00:00","purseUsa":400000,"positionAtFinish":1},{"trackName":"SARATOGA","raceName":"Mahony S.","grade":"3","raceDate":"August, 16 2026 00:00:00","purseUsa":225000,"positionAtFinish":1},{"trackName":"SARATOGA","raceName":"Quick Call S. Presented by the Thoroughbred Retirement Foundation","grade":"3","raceDate":"July, 19 2026 00:00:00","purseUsa":225000,"positionAtFinish":4},{"trackName":"SARATOGA","raceName":"Woody Stephens S. Presented by Mohegan Sun","grade":"1","raceDate":"June, 06 2026 00:00:00","purseUsa":500000,"positionAtFinish":6},{"trackName":"OAKLAWN PARK","raceName":"Bachelor S.","grade":" ","raceDate":"May, 01 2026 00:00:00","purseUsa":150000,"positionAtFinish":2},{"trackName":"OAKLAWN PARK","raceName":" ","grade":" ","raceDate":"March, 05 2026 00:00:00","purseUsa":125000,"positionAtFinish":1},{"trackName":"CHURCHILL DOWNS","raceName":"Ed Brown S.","grade":" ","raceDate":"November, 29 2025 00:00:00","purseUsa":225000,"positionAtFinish":3},{"trackName":"CHURCHILL DOWNS","raceName":" ","grade":" ","raceDate":"October, 26 2025 00:00:00","purseUsa":120000,"positionAtFinish":1},{"trackName":"BELMONT AT THE BIG A","raceName":"Champagne S.","grade":"1","raceDate":"October, 04 2025 00:00:00","purseUsa":500000,"positionAtFinish":5},{"trackName":"SARATOGA","raceName":" ","grade":" ","raceDate":"August, 30 2025 00:00:00","purseUsa":100000,"positionAtFinish":2},{"trackName":"SARATOGA","raceName":" ","grade":" ","raceDate":"July, 19 2025 00:00:00","purseUsa":100000,"positionAtFinish":3}],"record":{"previousYear":{"starts":5,"earnings":143800,"show":2,"win":1,"place":1,"showP":"40","winP":"20","placeP":"20"},"breedersCup":{"starts":0,"earnings":0,"show":0,"win":0,"place":0,"showP":"NA","winP":"NA","placeP":"NA"},"currentYear":{"starts":6,"earnings":466500,"show":0,"win":3,"place":1,"showP":"0","winP":"50","placeP":"17"},"lifetime":{"starts":11,"earnings":610300,"show":2,"win":4,"place":2,"showP":"18","winP":"36","placeP":"18"}},"yearlySummary":[{"showsP":"0","winsP":"50","placesP":"17","starts":6,"earnings":466500,"racingYear":2026,"shows":0,"wins":3,"places":1},{"showsP":"40","winsP":"20","placesP":"20","starts":5,"earnings":143800,"racingYear":2025,"shows":2,"wins":1,"places":1}],"morningLineOdds":[],"bio":"\u003cp\u003eStradale, a Yaupon colt trained by Steve Asmussen, spent the first 12 months of his career competing on dirt tracks from Saratoga to Aqueduct to Churchill Downs to Oaklawn Park, with mixed results. A surface switch finally seemed to switch him on. \r\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eHe was still winless when he lined up for the Champagne Stakes (G1) at the Belmont at the Big A meeting in October 2025 and finished fifth. He graduated in his next start three weeks later in Louisville and ran third in the Ed Brown Stakes a month after that. \r\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eStradale started 2026 with an allowance win at Oaklawn, then finished second in the Bachelor Stakes, beaten just a neck. He then returned to the top ranks, still on the dirt, in the Woody Stephens Stakes (G1) at Saratoga but finished a dull sixth. \r\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eFinally on the grass for the Quick Call Stakes (G3) at Saratoga July 19, Stradale showed some spark, rallying from ninth to a fourth-place finish, beaten only 3 lengths. \r\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eHe delivered on that promise in his next start, the Mahony Stakes (G3) Aug. 16 on the Saratoga green, taking a daylight lead in the stretch before holding on to win by a neck. \r\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eStradale returned to the dirt on Sept. 19 at Parx for the 6-furlong Gallant Bob (G2) and delivered as the favorite in the field of nine. Taking command at the eighth pole, Stradale opened a daylight advantage and won by 1 1/4 lengths over a fast-closing Dr. Kapur.\u003c/p\u003e","gradedStakesPoints":4,"regionWinnerBadges":[],"breederName":"Richard Bremer \u0026 Cheryl Sprick","uid":"blt1cd386ef5296b567","hasAutogeneratedPage":true,"url":"/redirect/horse/blt1cd386ef5296b567?ht=pre-entries","pageTitle":"Stradale","jockeyName":"","ownerName":"Kaleem Shah, Inc. (Kaleem Shah)","trainer":"Steven M. Asmussen","country":{"uid":"blt1af49e3a6a89373f","title":"USA","abbreviation":"USA","flag":{"src":"https://images.contentstack.io/v3/assets/blt9b0ea57b1efe7a70/blt9de45bbdff160673/60d219911e0505677a882fa1/USAFlag.png"}},"horseName":"Stradale","avatar":{"src":"https://images.contentstack.io/v3/assets/blt9b0ea57b1efe7a70/bltcb83d86fa670c76e/6ac132f90f65d89cd1bf1daa/Contender_Photo_Stradale_.jpg"},"regularImage":{"src":"https://images.contentstack.io/v3/assets/blt9b0ea57b1efe7a70/bltcb83d86fa670c76e/6ac132f90f65d89cd1bf1daa/Contender_Photo_Stradale_.jpg"},"ct